e6: ask-socket -> frontend streams
	step=s5
	message=async
	fragment=loop:every delta
	operand=[until the turn ends]
	status=proposed, pending user review
	note=output: key, output
	description=emit may run on the executor thread, so it hands the message to the server loop. A closed socket drops the message. The frontend adds a new key as a new output and replaces a known key in place, so growing prose stays in one output.
